1
00:01:11,740 --> 00:01:13,070
Is that normal?

2
00:01:13,240 --> 00:01:14,240
No.

3
00:01:16,910 --> 00:01:18,910
- Someone's hacking the system. 
- What?

4
00:01:19,080 --> 00:01:20,580
The containment tank 
is destabilizing.

5
00:01:21,250 --> 00:01:22,410
He's waking up.

6
00:03:27,790 --> 00:03:29,250
2024?

7
00:03:29,460 --> 00:03:32,790
I've been trapped for 50 years?

8
00:03:36,800 --> 00:03:37,880
- Move, move! 
- Take positions!

9
00:03:41,350 --> 00:03:42,720
Get on the ground now!

10
00:03:44,060 --> 00:03:45,680
We've got you surrounded!

11
00:03:55,230 --> 00:03:57,320
Okay, Captain, we got a 
rogue alien on the loose.

12
00:03:57,530 --> 00:03:59,030
How do we find 
him?

13
00:04:03,660 --> 00:04:06,290
Finally, 
some action!

14
00:04:06,500 --> 00:04:08,330
Okay, time to gear up.

15
00:04:08,500 --> 00:04:10,540
We're 
over the drop zone.

16
00:04:10,710 --> 00:04:13,210
All right, here 
we go. Showtime!

17
00:04:23,050 --> 00:04:25,100
What happened here?

18
00:04:25,260 --> 00:04:27,180
Looks like GUN 
got their butts kicked.

19
00:04:38,150 --> 00:04:40,740
Whoa! Are you guys seeing this?

20
00:04:40,900 --> 00:04:43,450
- He looks just like you. 
- Impossible!

21
00:04:43,450 --> 00:04:46,030
Walk away, before you get hurt.

22
00:04:46,200 --> 00:04:47,830
Whoa, whoa, easy, buddy.

23
00:04:49,120 --> 00:04:50,870
We don't want to fight you.

24
00:04:51,040 --> 00:04:53,750
Actually, Sonic, I 
would like to fight.

25
00:04:53,920 --> 00:04:55,340
Not now.

26
00:04:55,540 --> 00:04:57,420
Why don't you stop throwing 
cars at us for a second

27
00:04:57,460 --> 00:04:58,880
and come down here to talk?

28
00:04:59,050 --> 00:05:01,630
You jumped out of 
a GUN helicopter.

29
00:05:01,630 --> 00:05:03,760
There's nothing to talk about.

30
00:05:03,930 --> 00:05:05,800
All right, then. Enough!

31
00:05:05,970 --> 00:05:07,180
Knuckles, no!

32
00:05:07,350 --> 00:05:09,930
Let us talk with our fists!

33
00:05:24,780 --> 00:05:25,950
Knuckles!

34
00:05:26,120 --> 00:05:28,290
Knuckles! Knuckles, 
are you okay?

35
00:05:28,490 --> 00:05:29,700
No, not really. Ow!

36
00:05:32,250 --> 00:05:33,790
Who is this guy?

37
00:05:33,960 --> 00:05:35,130
He is much more impressive

38
00:05:35,290 --> 00:05:37,130
than the hedgehog I 
fought previously.

39
00:05:37,290 --> 00:05:39,210
Dude,
I'm standing right here

40
00:05:39,210 --> 00:05:42,510
Now come on, he can't take us all at once

41
00:05:43,130 --> 00:05:44,930
Ow!

42
00:05:52,600 --> 00:05:53,600
Weakling.

43
00:05:57,480 --> 00:05:59,110
Don't try to follow me.

44
00:06:02,900 --> 00:06:05,030
Sonic, I know that look.

45
00:06:05,200 --> 00:06:07,030
Going after him is a bad idea.

46
00:06:26,680 --> 00:06:28,140
Coming through!

47
00:06:35,480 --> 00:06:36,810
Watch out!

48
00:06:40,820 --> 00:06:41,940
Yah!

49
00:07:24,320 --> 00:07:25,070
Sonic!

50
00:07:25,240 --> 00:07:26,400
Are you okay?

51
00:07:26,990 --> 00:07:29,240
Sorry, buddy. I'm still 
working on this teamwork thing.

52
00:07:29,410 --> 00:07:30,910
So now what?

53
00:07:31,070 --> 00:07:33,290
Well, I'm not jumping out 
of any more helicopters

54
00:07:33,450 --> 00:07:35,450
until we get some 
answers from GUN.

55
00:07:35,620 --> 00:07:37,210
We need somewhere to regroup.

56
00:07:38,710 --> 00:07:40,540
I know just the place.

57
00:07:50,340 --> 00:07:51,640
Commander Walters!

58
00:07:51,930 --> 00:07:52,970
Sonic.

59
00:07:54,060 --> 00:07:56,810
Thank God you're all okay. 
I'm sure you have questions.

60
00:07:57,100 --> 00:07:58,520
Who was that guy?

61
00:07:58,690 --> 00:08:01,350
Shadow's story began a 
lot like yours, Sonic.

62
00:08:01,560 --> 00:08:04,320
But where you found family 
and friends on this planet,

63
00:08:04,520 --> 00:08:08,030
Shadow found only pain and loss.

64
00:08:08,780 --> 00:08:11,110
<i>It begins over 50 years ago,</i>

65
00:08:11,280 --> 00:08:14,410
<i>with a meteor crash in a 
quiet corner of Oklahoma.</i>

66
00:08:14,620 --> 00:08:18,210
<i>The meteorite 
contained a life-form.</i>

67
00:08:20,960 --> 00:08:22,750
<i>The ultimate life-form.</i>

68
00:08:24,750 --> 00:08:27,210
<i>Shadow's power... 
his "chaos energy"...</i>

69
00:08:27,380 --> 00:08:30,380
<i>went far beyond any 
living creature.</i>

70
00:08:33,010 --> 00:08:35,600
<i>The scientist who discovered 
him believed this power</i>

71
00:08:35,760 --> 00:08:37,930
<i>would usher in a new 
era for humanity.</i>

72
00:08:39,430 --> 00:08:42,600
<i>But Shadow's power 
proved too dangerous.</i>

73
00:08:45,520 --> 00:08:47,530
<i>A terrible accident 
destroyed the lab,</i>

74
00:08:47,690 --> 00:08:49,950
<i>taking human lives 
with it.</i>

75
00:08:50,110 --> 00:08:54,370
<i>The project leader was blamed 
for the incident and imprisoned.</i>

76
00:08:54,570 --> 00:08:56,280
<i>With the program 
canceled...</i>

77
00:08:56,370 --> 00:08:59,330
<i>Shadow was a loose end no 
one knew how to deal with.</i>

78
00:09:00,620 --> 00:09:02,540
<i>Too dangerous to 
be walking free,</i>

79
00:09:02,710 --> 00:09:05,040
<i>too valuable to destroy.</i>

80
00:09:06,130 --> 00:09:08,210
<i>So I had him placed 
into stasis</i>

81
00:09:11,380 --> 00:09:14,470
Wait a second. If Shadow's 
been on ice for 50 years,

82
00:09:14,640 --> 00:09:16,930
- someone had to help him escape. 
- True.

83
00:09:16,180 --> 00:09:18,720
But there's only a few 
people in the world

84
00:09:18,930 --> 00:09:20,770
who even know of 
Shadow's existence.

85
00:09:38,990 --> 00:09:39,120
Get down!

86
00:09:54,720 --> 00:09:55,970
Egg drones?

87
00:09:56,140 --> 00:09:58,850
But Robotnik is 
supposed to be dead!

88
00:10:32,920 --> 00:10:33,920
Commander Walters!

89
00:10:35,470 --> 00:10:37,510
Commander 
Walters, are you okay?

90
00:10:38,720 --> 00:10:39,720
Sonic...

91
00:10:42,310 --> 00:10:43,430
take this.

92
00:10:43,600 --> 00:10:45,640
What is 
it? A key...

93
00:10:46,900 --> 00:10:49,440
to the most powerful 
weapon GUN has ever built.

94
00:10:49,610 --> 00:10:52,150
You're the only one I 
trust to keep it safe.

95
00:10:54,190 --> 00:10:55,490
Commander Walters...

96
00:11:04,330 --> 00:11:05,830
Alpha team, fan out!

97
00:11:07,210 --> 00:11:08,580
Do we have eyes?

98
00:11:09,250 --> 00:11:10,250
Secure the perimeter!

99
00:11:13,550 --> 00:11:14,920
Medevac is en route.

100
00:11:18,760 --> 00:11:20,220
His launch key is missing.

101
00:11:23,260 --> 00:11:24,720
Why are we 
running from GUN?

102
00:11:24,890 --> 00:11:26,390
Aren't we on the same team?

103
00:11:26,560 --> 00:11:27,980
Until we get 
more information,

104
00:11:27,980 --> 00:11:29,690
we're not trusting anyone.

105
00:11:29,850 --> 00:11:31,560
- Follow me. 
- Get it... off!

106
00:11:49,460 --> 00:11:50,830
Who are you?

107
00:11:53,710 --> 00:11:56,050
It's the Goat Milker!

108
00:11:56,710 --> 00:11:58,760
Relax. I'm not here to fight.

109
00:11:58,930 --> 00:12:01,970
- Then why are you here? 
- And why did you free Shadow?

110
00:12:01,260 --> 00:12:04,060
Are you kidding?

111
00:12:04,220 --> 00:12:07,850
The last thing we want is more 
super-powered hedgehogs running around.

112
00:12:08,020 --> 00:12:09,980
The doctor had 
nothing to do with it.

113
00:12:11,690 --> 00:12:13,520
And I can prove 
it.

114
00:12:28,910 --> 00:12:29,620
Please,

115
00:12:30,710 --> 00:12:31,750
join me in the crab.

116
00:12:32,290 --> 00:12:33,710
<i>Pablo!</i>

117
00:12:35,630 --> 00:12:37,050
!¡Bastardo!

118
00:12:37,210 --> 00:12:39,590
Buenos días, !¡hermano!

119
00:12:39,760 --> 00:12:40,930
<i>No!</i>

120
00:12:43,390 --> 00:12:45,680
Let that be a 
lesson to you, Juan.

121
00:12:45,890 --> 00:12:47,430
Family

122
00:12:47,600 --> 00:12:50,850
is a field of 
emotional claymores

123
00:12:51,020 --> 00:12:53,230
that leave you 
abandoned, betrayed

124
00:12:55,020 --> 00:12:57,900
and weeping while you eat cake,

125
00:12:58,070 --> 00:13:00,450
which creates copious 
amounts of adipose tissue,

126
00:13:00,610 --> 00:13:03,620
and what some calloused 
individuals refer to as...

127
00:13:03,780 --> 00:13:06,410
man boobs.

128
00:13:06,580 --> 00:13:07,740
Ha.

129
00:13:25,550 --> 00:13:27,600
Doctor, we have visitors.

130
00:13:29,100 --> 00:13:31,100
Really?

131
00:13:31,270 --> 00:13:33,980
I thought I was having an 
anthropomorphic nightmare.

132
00:13:34,150 --> 00:13:35,770
Where the only person I 
could trust in the world

133
00:13:35,770 --> 00:13:37,320
showed up with all 
my worst enemies,

134
00:13:37,480 --> 00:13:39,190
while I was in a bathrobe,

135
00:13:39,360 --> 00:13:41,610
playing congas on 
my big, fat belly!

136
00:13:41,780 --> 00:13:43,070
Sorry, sir.

137
00:13:43,240 --> 00:13:45,370
I don't believe 
it. Eggman's alive?

138
00:13:45,530 --> 00:13:47,910
And he's never looked worse.

139
00:13:48,080 --> 00:13:50,370
Well, maybe,

140
00:13:50,540 --> 00:13:54,420
this is what not giving a damn what 
you think I look like looks like.

141
00:13:54,580 --> 00:13:57,790
Sir, right now we have 
an even bigger problem.

142
00:13:58,000 --> 00:13:59,380
Oh, come on.

143
00:14:01,510 --> 00:14:03,800
There's an imposter out 
there using your technology.

144
00:14:04,010 --> 00:14:07,300
Imposter. That's 
impossi... What?

145
00:14:07,470 --> 00:14:08,970
No.

146
00:14:08,220 --> 00:14:13,180
My sweet mechanized spawn!

147
00:14:13,350 --> 00:14:16,980
Whomever this party-pooping 
posse is looking for

148
00:14:17,150 --> 00:14:19,440
has stolen my persona

149
00:14:19,610 --> 00:14:22,990
and the precious 
babies from my egg sac.

150
00:14:23,650 --> 00:14:25,150
Well...

151
00:14:25,320 --> 00:14:29,700
I'll soon egg-xact my revenge.

152
00:14:29,870 --> 00:14:31,540
You see what I did 
there?

153
00:14:31,700 --> 00:14:34,960
It's time for the 
dramatic soap-opera twist,

154
00:14:35,120 --> 00:14:39,250
where this Pablo 
reveals his Juan!

155
00:14:39,420 --> 00:14:43,300
By cross-referencing 
the precise coordinates

156
00:14:43,460 --> 00:14:46,220
of each drone's energy spikes,

157
00:14:46,970 --> 00:14:49,100
I can track my babies

158
00:14:49,260 --> 00:14:51,850
to the imposter's 
base of operations,

159
00:14:52,060 --> 00:14:53,430
right about...

160
00:14:53,600 --> 00:14:54,430
there!

161
00:14:55,180 --> 00:14:57,230
All right, Egghead. 
I hate to say it,

162
00:14:57,400 --> 00:14:58,980
but it looks like 
we're partners.

163
00:15:00,110 --> 00:15:02,030
On one condition.

164
00:15:03,480 --> 00:15:06,070
Dude, you have serious issues.

165
00:15:06,240 --> 00:15:07,320
Ow!

166
00:15:11,160 --> 00:15:12,330
Let's...

167
00:15:13,120 --> 00:15:14,250
do this!

168
00:15:40,610 --> 00:15:41,860
Suck it in!

169
00:15:44,360 --> 00:15:45,740
Tinker-tailor?

170
00:15:45,900 --> 00:15:47,320
I need room.

171
00:15:47,490 --> 00:15:50,160
Think Elvis, circa 1976.

172
00:15:50,320 --> 00:15:52,580
But sir, I don't have 
the proper materials.

173
00:15:53,620 --> 00:15:54,990
Found some.

174
00:15:57,500 --> 00:15:58,710
Resourceful.

175
00:16:39,210 --> 00:16:40,370
Hey! This is a restricted area.

176
00:16:41,460 --> 00:16:43,750
Oh, it's okay. She's the 
professor's granddaughter.

177
00:16:43,920 --> 00:16:46,050
He takes her everywhere.

178
00:16:46,210 --> 00:16:49,300
Welcome to the lab, Maria. 
I'm Captain Walters.

179
00:16:49,470 --> 00:16:50,880
Oh, do you know 
where my room is?

180
00:16:51,050 --> 00:16:52,590
Yeah, down the hall 
and to the right.

181
00:16:52,800 --> 00:16:54,300
Make yourself at home.

182
00:16:54,470 --> 00:16:55,640
But, um,

183
00:16:55,850 --> 00:16:57,600
let's lose the 
skates, okay, kiddo?

184
00:16:57,810 --> 00:16:59,230
Okay.

185
00:19:19,450 --> 00:19:20,620
Look out!

186
00:20:33,060 --> 00:20:34,770
Professor?

187
00:20:34,940 --> 00:20:37,990
It's good to see you, Shadow.

188
00:20:38,150 --> 00:20:40,240
I knew you'd come home.

189
00:20:40,400 --> 00:20:42,990
I can't get her out of my head.

190
00:20:43,160 --> 00:20:44,700
The pain...

191
00:20:44,870 --> 00:20:46,200
It's too much.

192
00:20:46,370 --> 00:20:49,870
And that is why we 
have to punish them.

193
00:20:59,090 --> 00:21:01,180
This door is 
six-inch-thick solid steel

194
00:21:01,340 --> 00:21:03,140
on a pressurized latch.

195
00:21:03,300 --> 00:21:05,470
I'll need a moment to 
calculate the molecular density

196
00:21:05,640 --> 00:21:07,270
and invert the 
venting mechanics.

197
00:21:10,940 --> 00:21:12,190
I unlocked it.

198
00:21:12,350 --> 00:21:15,360
Subtle as 
always, fist-for-brains.

199
00:21:16,610 --> 00:21:18,360
Easy, Shadow.

200
00:21:18,530 --> 00:21:21,030
Those are the guests 
I've been expecting.

201
00:21:21,200 --> 00:21:23,820
Let's give them a warm welcome.

202
00:21:27,660 --> 00:21:28,160
Whoa.

203
00:21:29,200 --> 00:21:30,450
What is this place?

204
00:21:30,620 --> 00:21:32,580
It looks 
like a military base,

205
00:21:32,750 --> 00:21:34,580
but nobody's been 
here for years.

206
00:21:36,130 --> 00:21:38,380
Just a dark, creepy hallway.

207
00:21:38,550 --> 00:21:40,210
Nothing to be afraid of.

208
00:21:41,970 --> 00:21:43,680
You hear that, ghost?

209
00:21:43,840 --> 00:21:45,390
You don't frighten me!

210
00:21:49,850 --> 00:21:52,230
Get... a... grip.

211
00:21:53,140 --> 00:21:54,900
Boo.

212
00:22:18,840 --> 00:22:22,380
Whoa. Look at all this stuff.

213
00:22:22,970 --> 00:22:24,430
He had a family.

214
00:22:24,970 --> 00:22:27,010
Is that what I smell?

215
00:22:27,010 --> 00:22:30,260
The stench of domestic harmony?

216
00:22:30,430 --> 00:22:33,980
You ever wonder what your life would 
have been like if you had a family?

217
00:22:34,140 --> 00:22:35,560
Hmm... No!

218
00:22:35,770 --> 00:22:37,770
Maybe you wouldn't have 
gone full supervillain.

219
00:22:37,940 --> 00:22:40,780
I have no parents, 
no aunts, no uncles.

220
00:22:40,940 --> 00:22:43,440
And something about my 
attitude renders me...

221
00:22:44,400 --> 00:22:48,530
undesirable to all 
possible genders.

222
00:22:50,410 --> 00:22:52,580
My future is a cul-de-sac!

223
00:22:53,580 --> 00:22:55,580
The Robotnik name ends...

224
00:22:57,250 --> 00:22:58,920
<i>avec moi.</i>

225
00:22:59,090 --> 00:23:01,130
Yes, I know French.

226
00:23:05,630 --> 00:23:06,760
Whoa.

227
00:23:06,930 --> 00:23:09,930
Is this where you 
grew up, Shadow?

228
00:23:10,100 --> 00:23:11,890
No wonder you're so mad.

229
00:23:13,720 --> 00:23:14,930
What happened here?

230
00:23:20,690 --> 00:23:22,070
Where'd you go, hedgehog?

231
00:23:22,270 --> 00:23:24,110
I wasn't finished 
trauma dumping.

232
00:23:25,950 --> 00:23:28,740
My darlings!

233
00:23:30,620 --> 00:23:33,040
My eggy weggies!

234
00:23:34,160 --> 00:23:37,250
<i>♪ Memories ♪</i>

235
00:23:37,420 --> 00:23:40,750
<i>♪ Light the corners ♪</i>

236
00:23:40,920 --> 00:23:44,590
<i>♪ Of my mind ♪</i>

237
00:23:44,760 --> 00:23:47,880
<i>♪ Misty watercolor ♪</i>

238
00:23:48,050 --> 00:23:53,680
<i>♪ Memories ♪</i>

239
00:23:53,850 --> 00:23:56,730
<i>♪ Of the way ♪</i>

240
00:23:56,890 --> 00:24:02,150
<i>♪ We weren't ♪</i>

241
00:24:03,110 --> 00:24:04,110
I...

242
00:24:05,860 --> 00:24:07,610
- don't believe it. 
- Don't you?

243
00:24:07,780 --> 00:24:09,030
- It's impossible. 
- Is it?

244
00:24:09,200 --> 00:24:10,280
- It couldn't be. 
- Couldn't it?

245
00:24:10,320 --> 00:24:11,070
I'm... Are you?

246
00:24:11,280 --> 00:24:12,450
Imposter!

247
00:24:12,620 --> 00:24:14,870
You stole my babies!

248
00:24:15,040 --> 00:24:18,210
But they know who 
their real daddy is...

249
00:24:18,410 --> 00:24:19,500
drone-napper!

250
00:24:21,380 --> 00:24:24,460
Magnificent creations, my boy.

251
00:24:24,630 --> 00:24:27,170
I borrowed them to lure you here

252
00:24:27,380 --> 00:24:29,380
and reunite our family.

253
00:24:31,090 --> 00:24:32,760
You see, Ivo...

254
00:24:34,890 --> 00:24:37,890
I'm your grandfather:

255
00:24:38,060 --> 00:24:40,520
Gerald Robotnik.

256
00:24:44,570 --> 00:24:47,230
My... grandfather?

257
00:24:48,990 --> 00:24:51,860
But how? And why?

258
00:24:52,660 --> 00:24:54,700
And who did what with whom?

259
00:24:54,870 --> 00:24:59,790
You hail from an 
ancestry of excellence...

260
00:24:59,960 --> 00:25:01,620
tied directly <i>à moi.</i>

261
00:25:02,710 --> 00:25:05,630
Yes, I know French.

262
00:25:08,130 --> 00:25:09,670
You do look like me.

263
00:25:10,630 --> 00:25:12,590
But fatter. And older.

264
00:25:13,470 --> 00:25:15,430
And there's that funny smell.

265
00:25:17,100 --> 00:25:19,930
But the resemblance is uncanny.

266
00:25:20,810 --> 00:25:22,440
It's as if...

267
00:25:22,600 --> 00:25:24,690
we're two 
characters in a movie

268
00:25:24,860 --> 00:25:27,440
being played by the same actor.

269
00:25:27,610 --> 00:25:30,030
- But I need real proof! 
- Ivo!

270
00:25:30,190 --> 00:25:31,530
We have very little time.

271
00:25:33,030 --> 00:25:35,160
But I could field a 
couple of queries.

272
00:25:35,370 --> 00:25:38,490
Name the most elegant 
formula in mathematics.

273
00:25:38,660 --> 00:25:39,100
Euler's Identity.

274
00:25:40,160 --> 00:25:42,500
E to the I times pi 
plus one equals zilch.

275
00:25:42,670 --> 00:25:44,500
European capitals 
arranged alphabetically

276
00:25:44,670 --> 00:25:45,920
by the fourth letter.

277
00:25:46,090 --> 00:25:47,840
Riga, Monaco, Sarajevo, Tirana.

278
00:25:48,000 --> 00:25:49,880
The speed of light divided 
by the speed of sound,

279
00:25:49,960 --> 00:25:52,010
divided by the speed of 
the bus in the movie <i>Speed.</i>

280
00:25:53,720 --> 00:25:56,260
17,893.33333...

281
00:25:56,470 --> 00:25:59,890
Rounding up? 17,894 MPH.

282
00:26:00,060 --> 00:26:02,560
And, for all the marbles...

283
00:26:02,730 --> 00:26:04,900
Good. I lost mine.

284
00:26:05,060 --> 00:26:07,110
A rare lung disease,

285
00:26:07,270 --> 00:26:10,400
and the longest word in 
the English dictionary.

286
00:26:11,030 --> 00:26:12,530
Um...

287
00:26:12,700 --> 00:26:15,990
Pneumonoultramicroscopic- 
silicovolcanoconiosis!

288
00:26:16,870 --> 00:26:20,540
- Pap-pap! 
- In the saggy flesh.

289
00:26:20,700 --> 00:26:22,790
But looking pretty good 
for a hundred and ten.

290
00:26:25,210 --> 00:26:27,840
Oh, Grampy-poo!

291
00:26:31,210 --> 00:26:35,010
Where have you been 
my entire life?

292
00:26:36,930 --> 00:26:38,930
Wait.

293
00:26:39,100 --> 00:26:41,310
Where have you been... 
my entire life?

294
00:26:41,520 --> 00:26:47,480
Locked in a top-secret 
prison for the last 50 years.

295
00:26:47,690 --> 00:26:50,940
Made it kind of hard to 
send Christmas cards.

296
00:26:51,110 --> 00:26:52,610
Now...

297
00:26:52,780 --> 00:26:56,320
you're probably wondering 
why I brought you here.

298
00:26:56,530 --> 00:26:57,910
You didn't bring me here!

299
00:26:58,070 --> 00:27:01,370
I used my unparalleled 
intellect to track you down.

300
00:27:01,580 --> 00:27:05,500
Per the plan I concocted with 
my unparalleled intellect.

301
00:27:05,660 --> 00:27:07,460
You'll see.

302
00:27:07,630 --> 00:27:10,170
I have the answer to everything.

303
00:27:11,800 --> 00:27:13,460
Come on, kiddo.

304
00:27:27,230 --> 00:27:29,190
Oh, no. Oh, no, no.

305
00:27:29,360 --> 00:27:31,190
Someone tell me 
this is some kind of

306
00:27:31,360 --> 00:27:33,530
concussion-induced nightmare.

307
00:27:33,650 --> 00:27:35,650
Double your villains, 
double your fun!

308
00:27:35,820 --> 00:27:38,610
Two Robotniks are 
way worse than one.

309
00:27:38,780 --> 00:27:39,780
Chest bump?

310
00:27:39,950 --> 00:27:40,950
No.

311
00:27:41,870 --> 00:27:43,950
Stone, why are you tied up?

312
00:27:44,160 --> 00:27:46,710
Do that on your own 
time. You sicken me.

313
00:27:46,870 --> 00:27:49,290
You must be the 
long-lost grandson.

314
00:27:49,460 --> 00:27:51,420
And you must be another 
stinking hedgehog.

315
00:27:52,500 --> 00:27:54,550
So you're the one 
behind all this.

316
00:27:54,710 --> 00:27:56,920
- The Shadow breakout. 
- The attack on Walters.

317
00:27:57,090 --> 00:27:58,300
That musty old-man smell.

318
00:27:58,470 --> 00:28:00,430
How dare you insult me

319
00:28:00,590 --> 00:28:02,260
with your unsolicited 
exposition!

320
00:28:02,430 --> 00:28:04,520
Shadow, get the key.

321
00:28:04,970 --> 00:28:06,390
Yep, we're that stupid.

322
00:28:06,600 --> 00:28:08,770
GUN took everything from us.

323
00:28:08,940 --> 00:28:11,860
And now we are going to 
take everything from them.

324
00:28:12,020 --> 00:28:13,270
With this.

325
00:28:13,440 --> 00:28:17,110
My masterpiece of malevolence...

326
00:28:17,280 --> 00:28:19,820
The Eclipse Cannon.

327
00:28:19,990 --> 00:28:23,080
<i>In exchange for my freedom,</i>

328
00:28:23,240 --> 00:28:25,370
<i>I gave GUN the most 
powerful weapon</i>

329
00:28:25,580 --> 00:28:28,080
<i>mankind has ever seen,</i>

330
00:28:28,250 --> 00:28:30,830
<i>capable of delivering 
a precision strike</i>

331
00:28:31,000 --> 00:28:32,380
<i>anywhere on Earth.</i>

332
00:28:33,840 --> 00:28:35,050
<i>Our first target:</i>

333
00:28:35,880 --> 00:28:37,510
<i>GUN Headquarters.</i>

334
00:28:37,720 --> 00:28:39,840
But firing a weapon 
that powerful

335
00:28:40,010 --> 00:28:41,970
could threaten millions 
of innocent lives!

336
00:28:42,140 --> 00:28:44,390
Yeah, tera-bite me.

337
00:28:44,600 --> 00:28:49,440
This is one of two keys required 
to launch the Eclipse Cannon.

338
00:28:49,640 --> 00:28:51,940
The other is locked 
inside GUN headquarters.

339
00:28:52,100 --> 00:28:53,980
Once we have both,

340
00:28:54,150 --> 00:28:56,980
I will take rightful 
control of my weapon.

341
00:28:57,150 --> 00:28:58,940
I'm in.

342
00:29:05,910 --> 00:29:07,370
Holy crab!

343
00:29:07,540 --> 00:29:09,160
Spacious 
and crustaceous.

344
00:29:10,080 --> 00:29:11,250
Thank you so much

345
00:29:11,420 --> 00:29:13,080
for inspiring this 
little adventure.

346
00:29:13,250 --> 00:29:15,420
It really worked out for me.

347
00:29:16,550 --> 00:29:18,710
Shadow, wait! Don't do this.

348
00:29:19,010 --> 00:29:23,260
I've spent 50 years reliving 
what they did to her.

349
00:29:58,340 --> 00:30:00,880
Yeah! Yes!

350
00:30:04,590 --> 00:30:05,590
Yikes.

351
00:30:09,060 --> 00:30:13,190
I've spent years trying 
to cleanse the cosmos

352
00:30:13,350 --> 00:30:17,020
of that spiny, blue speed freak.

353
00:30:17,190 --> 00:30:18,820
And you did it...

354
00:30:20,360 --> 00:30:22,190
in one afternoon.

355
00:30:22,360 --> 00:30:26,280
There's nothing we can't 
destroy together, my boy.

356
00:30:26,450 --> 00:30:29,330
Charting route to GUN 
Headquarters in London, sirs.

357
00:30:29,490 --> 00:30:31,580
ETA four hours.

358
00:30:31,750 --> 00:30:33,080
As the crab flies.

359
00:30:33,250 --> 00:30:35,580
By all accounts, we're 
ahead of schedule.

360
00:30:36,540 --> 00:30:38,460
We should take this time

361
00:30:38,630 --> 00:30:40,630
to get to know 
each other better.

362
00:30:40,800 --> 00:30:42,550
Wow. What?

363
00:30:43,300 --> 00:30:44,380
You mean...

364
00:30:44,550 --> 00:30:47,800
spend some qua-qua-quality time?

365
00:30:47,970 --> 00:30:52,720
You've waited for 
this your whole life.

366
00:30:52,890 --> 00:30:58,900
How would you choose to spend one 
perfect day with your new grand pal?

367
00:31:53,120 --> 00:31:56,410
Ooh!

368
00:32:41,250 --> 00:32:43,040
London, baby!

369
00:32:46,340 --> 00:32:48,840
GUN Headquarters is right there.

370
00:32:49,010 --> 00:32:52,970
Let me go in, get the key 
and destroy anyone in my way!

371
00:32:53,140 --> 00:32:54,720
I want revenge.

372
00:32:53,970 --> 00:32:56,260
Patience, Shadow.

373
00:32:56,430 --> 00:32:58,680
Just let us handle this...

374
00:32:59,690 --> 00:33:02,980
and I promise 
you'll have revenge

375
00:33:03,150 --> 00:33:06,900
on a scale you couldn't 
possibly imagine.

376
00:33:07,070 --> 00:33:10,070
Come on, Granddaddy-O, 
we've got...

377
00:33:10,280 --> 00:33:11,320
dirt to do!

378
00:33:11,490 --> 00:33:13,280
Suits.

379
00:33:13,450 --> 00:33:14,450
Right here, sir.

380
00:33:15,490 --> 00:33:17,370
Stone, babysit the hedgehog.

381
00:33:17,540 --> 00:33:19,960
Keep the crab on a low boil.

382
00:33:21,120 --> 00:33:23,460
It's time for more 
family bonding.

383
00:33:26,630 --> 00:33:28,880
Tom, Maddie, are you 
in position and ready?

384
00:33:29,050 --> 00:33:31,170
- We were born ready. 
- Let's do this.

385
00:33:31,340 --> 00:33:32,590
<i>Knuckles, 
how about you?</i>

386
00:33:32,720 --> 00:33:34,890
I have taken my perch 
atop the giant clock.

387
00:33:35,050 --> 00:33:36,890
All right, everyone 
knows what to do.

388
00:33:37,060 --> 00:33:39,140
Tom and Maddie, you guys 
plant the USB drive.

389
00:33:39,310 --> 00:33:41,850
I'll disable the traps. Sonic 
will snag the launch key.

390
00:33:42,020 --> 00:33:43,770
And Knuckles, you stand by to...

391
00:33:43,940 --> 00:33:46,270
Break glass in 
case of emergency.

392
00:33:46,440 --> 00:33:47,480
Then we're all set.

393
00:33:47,650 --> 00:33:48,360
Hologram time.

394
00:33:50,780 --> 00:33:51,780
You go first.

395
00:34:03,420 --> 00:34:04,830
Okay, Tails, what 
are we looking for?

396
00:34:05,040 --> 00:34:08,380
<i>The security server is in 
the 7th row, 23rd cabinet.</i>

397
00:34:08,920 --> 00:34:11,420
All right, hang tight, guys. 
Maddie's about to insert the drive.

398
00:34:11,510 --> 00:34:12,510
Ready?

399
00:34:12,670 --> 00:34:13,840
<i>Three...</i>

400
00:34:14,010 --> 00:34:15,180
<i>two...</i>

401
00:34:15,340 --> 00:34:16,600
<i>one...</i>

402
00:34:18,180 --> 00:34:19,430
Go.

403
00:34:21,270 --> 00:34:23,060
I'm shutting down the 
outside sensors now.

404
00:34:23,230 --> 00:34:24,600
Yes! Uh...

405
00:34:24,770 --> 00:34:27,060
Hold on. Is...

406
00:34:27,230 --> 00:34:28,980
there supposed to be 
another USB drive here?

407
00:34:29,020 --> 00:34:31,570
One with a 
giant mustache on it?

408
00:34:31,740 --> 00:34:34,990
Oh, no. I've got two heat 
signatures en route to the vault.

409
00:34:35,160 --> 00:34:36,530
Which can only mean...

410
00:34:42,950 --> 00:34:46,120
The Robotniks have 
entered the chat.

411
00:34:46,210 --> 00:34:48,080
Hello! What's this?

412
00:34:48,250 --> 00:34:50,840
I knew I saw an outside signal!

413
00:34:51,000 --> 00:34:52,880
<i>Cheerio!</i>

414
00:34:53,050 --> 00:34:55,010
<i>I guess someone forgot to flush.</i>

415
00:35:15,990 --> 00:35:18,870
What now, my cunning cohort?

416
00:35:19,030 --> 00:35:20,530
Just a little teamwork!

417
00:35:28,460 --> 00:35:29,630
Hey...

418
00:35:30,290 --> 00:35:31,670
The lasers...

419
00:35:32,800 --> 00:35:34,460
don't seem to be 
penetrating my suit.

420
00:35:36,760 --> 00:35:39,800
They're conforming to the 
shape of my bodacious bod.

421
00:35:39,970 --> 00:35:41,390
Of course.

422
00:35:43,560 --> 00:35:45,230
I designed these suits 
to create a field

423
00:35:45,390 --> 00:35:47,480
of laser-bending 
thermal distortion.

424
00:35:47,640 --> 00:35:49,560
Wasn't sure it 
would work till now.

425
00:35:49,770 --> 00:35:51,190
You're heartless, son.

426
00:35:51,360 --> 00:35:53,230
- Hmm! 
- Rotten to the core.

427
00:35:53,400 --> 00:35:55,110
- Mm-hmm. 
- I'm...

428
00:35:55,280 --> 00:35:56,490
so proud.

429
00:35:56,650 --> 00:35:59,030
So now we can just 
dance right through.

430
00:36:01,620 --> 00:36:03,700
That sounds like a challenge.

431
00:36:48,750 --> 00:36:50,710
The Robotniks are 
almost at the vault!

432
00:36:50,870 --> 00:36:52,960
We're out of time. I'm going.

433
00:36:53,170 --> 00:36:54,290
No, Sonic!

434
00:36:54,460 --> 00:36:55,750
I haven't disabled 
the traps yet!

435
00:37:01,890 --> 00:37:03,220
You're not gonna make it!

436
00:37:03,430 --> 00:37:04,430
I can make it.

437
00:37:07,930 --> 00:37:09,350
You're not gonna make it!

438
00:37:09,520 --> 00:37:10,690
I'm gonna make it.

439
00:37:21,910 --> 00:37:24,530
Our destiny awaits.

440
00:37:25,620 --> 00:37:27,450
Stop right there, Roboscum!

441
00:37:27,620 --> 00:37:29,830
- Let's do this! 
- Copy!

442
00:37:37,130 --> 00:37:38,710
Too slow, Eggmen.

443
00:37:38,880 --> 00:37:41,220
Now if you don't mind, 
I've got to get that key.

444
00:37:42,300 --> 00:37:43,510
Whoa!

445
00:37:43,510 --> 00:37:46,600
this vault is armed 
with variable gravity.

446
00:37:48,140 --> 00:37:48,970
No kidding.

447
00:37:49,140 --> 00:37:50,930
Green goes up...

448
00:37:51,100 --> 00:37:53,270
and red takes you down... hard.

449
00:37:53,480 --> 00:37:54,650
Rockwell, listen to me.

450
00:37:54,810 --> 00:37:56,610
The Robotniks are 
planning to...

451
00:37:56,770 --> 00:37:58,820
Oh, they're planning on stealing 
a second key, just like you are?

452
00:37:58,860 --> 00:38:00,240
Yes, I'm aware.

453
00:38:01,780 --> 00:38:04,280
I called it the second 
Commander Walters was attacked.

454
00:38:04,490 --> 00:38:05,950
So...

455
00:38:06,120 --> 00:38:08,700
thank you for taking the bait

456
00:38:08,870 --> 00:38:10,370
and falling right into my trap.

457
00:38:10,540 --> 00:38:12,660
I don't believe this.

458
00:38:12,830 --> 00:38:14,460
I know, grandson.

459
00:38:14,620 --> 00:38:16,630
A woman in the military!

460
00:38:18,550 --> 00:38:19,960
Let's go.

461
00:38:21,050 --> 00:38:22,260
Go, positions!

462
00:38:22,470 --> 00:38:23,550
Full perimeter.

463
00:38:25,090 --> 00:38:26,430
Robotnik.

464
00:38:26,590 --> 00:38:28,850
Going full spandex, 
huh? Who's the fossil?

465
00:38:29,010 --> 00:38:33,140
That's my grandfather, you 
dough-eating dimbecile.

466
00:38:33,310 --> 00:38:36,440
- Who are they? 
- A couple of bleeding hearts,

467
00:38:36,600 --> 00:38:39,440
here to rescue their 
emotional-support animals.

468
00:38:39,610 --> 00:38:41,400
Enough! It's over.

469
00:38:41,570 --> 00:38:45,110
The only way you're leaving 
here is in handcuffs.

470
00:38:45,280 --> 00:38:46,990
There is no other way out.

471
00:38:47,280 --> 00:38:49,200
Hey, big guy, 
I think it's time to...

472
00:38:50,370 --> 00:38:53,660
Break glass in 
case of emergency!

473
00:39:00,800 --> 00:39:03,840
Ha! Nothing can 
stop Team Knuckles!

474
00:39:04,050 --> 00:39:05,130
Open fire!

475
00:39:06,130 --> 00:39:08,010
Knuckles, 
turn this stuff off!

476
00:39:08,180 --> 00:39:09,470
- Hurry! 
- On it.

477
00:39:11,100 --> 00:39:12,180
Uh-oh.

478
00:39:27,110 --> 00:39:29,160
- Can you move? 
- No, not at all.

479
00:39:29,320 --> 00:39:31,790
- Tails, can you? 
- No, I'm stuck.

480
00:39:31,950 --> 00:39:33,330
We might be here a while.

481
00:39:35,710 --> 00:39:37,960
Whoa! Whoa. Whoa. Whoa.

482
00:39:38,960 --> 00:39:40,380
Where's the key?

483
00:39:45,380 --> 00:39:47,550
Whoa!

484
00:39:47,720 --> 00:39:49,430
- What was that? 
- We might have a problem.

485
00:39:52,010 --> 00:39:53,970
No, no, no, no!

486
00:40:14,700 --> 00:40:16,790
I'm moving.

487
00:40:17,580 --> 00:40:19,170
I'm moving!

488
00:40:22,340 --> 00:40:24,800
You go get it, grandson!

489
00:40:24,880 --> 00:40:26,710
Oh, whoa, whoa...

490
00:40:29,220 --> 00:40:31,090
No. No, no!

491
00:40:31,720 --> 00:40:33,390
I'm almost there!

492
00:40:36,220 --> 00:40:37,020
Whoa!

493
00:40:53,870 --> 00:40:56,200
That was so not worth it!

494
00:40:58,620 --> 00:41:00,370
- You okay? 
- Yeah. You good?

495
00:41:00,540 --> 00:41:01,290
Sonic!

496
00:41:01,460 --> 00:41:03,290
Hey.

497
00:41:04,170 --> 00:41:05,460
Thanks for the save.

498
00:41:05,630 --> 00:41:07,300
Cutting it a little 
close, don't you think?

499
00:41:08,590 --> 00:41:09,920
Secure the room!

500
00:41:11,930 --> 00:41:13,180
She's got the key.

501
00:41:15,890 --> 00:41:16,970
I got an idea.

502
00:41:26,230 --> 00:41:27,650
Commander Walters.

503
00:41:27,820 --> 00:41:28,900
Sir.

504
00:41:29,110 --> 00:41:30,700
You're... Still alive?

505
00:41:30,860 --> 00:41:33,660
I'll die before I let that 
key fall into the wrong hands.

506
00:41:34,530 --> 00:41:35,910
Thanks for keeping it safe.

507
00:41:36,120 --> 00:41:37,580
I'll take it from here.

508
00:41:40,290 --> 00:41:42,120
That's an order, 
Director Rockwell.

509
00:41:45,790 --> 00:41:48,460
Now, organize the 
reinforcements.

510
00:41:49,800 --> 00:41:50,880
Yes, sir.

511
00:41:56,640 --> 00:41:58,850
Guys, guys, I got the key. 
I repeat, I got the key.

512
00:41:59,020 --> 00:42:00,640
Now let's get out of here.

513
00:42:04,850 --> 00:42:07,150
Commander Walters.

514
00:42:07,320 --> 00:42:08,980
No, no. No. Wait!

515
00:42:23,290 --> 00:42:24,710
What?

516
00:42:24,870 --> 00:42:27,420
Tom! Everyone's clear! 
Come on, let's go!

517
00:42:27,590 --> 00:42:29,460
You. What are you...

518
00:42:31,170 --> 00:42:32,220
Tom!

519
00:42:33,340 --> 00:42:35,390
Tom. Tom, what happened?

520
00:42:35,590 --> 00:42:38,640
Please, please, please get up. 
Hey, come on, please wake up.

521
00:42:39,430 --> 00:42:40,850
Wake up, wake up, wake up!

522
00:42:41,560 --> 00:42:42,980
Maria.

523
00:42:47,020 --> 00:42:48,730
What did you do?

524
00:42:50,940 --> 00:42:52,990
What I had to.

525
00:42:55,660 --> 00:42:57,320
Oh, my God. Tom!

526
00:43:00,580 --> 00:43:02,250
Help me up, kid.

527
00:43:05,080 --> 00:43:06,370
Freeze! Don't move!

528
00:43:06,580 --> 00:43:11,420
Any tricks up your sleeve, 
Captain Grandtastic?

529
00:43:18,180 --> 00:43:20,220
We got what we came for.

530
00:43:20,970 --> 00:43:23,850
Great job, Shadow.

531
00:43:24,600 --> 00:43:27,440
We have both keys.

532
00:43:27,650 --> 00:43:30,400
So where's your little 
science project?

533
00:43:31,820 --> 00:43:35,780
It's closer than 
you think, my boy.

534
00:43:37,950 --> 00:43:39,450
Welcome...

535
00:43:39,660 --> 00:43:42,990
to my masterpiece!

536
00:43:45,910 --> 00:43:47,670
I must hand it to GUN.

537
00:43:47,830 --> 00:43:50,340
They built her to my 
exact specifications.

538
00:43:51,420 --> 00:43:52,630
It's...

539
00:43:54,260 --> 00:43:55,840
remarkable!

540
00:43:56,010 --> 00:43:57,220
Mm-hmm.

541
00:43:57,380 --> 00:44:00,220
- Astounding! 
- Yes.

542
00:44:01,350 --> 00:44:03,470
That's my genius grand-genome!

543
00:44:03,680 --> 00:44:07,270
And I have one more surprise.

544
00:44:09,770 --> 00:44:13,780
It's a new suit!

545
00:44:43,680 --> 00:44:46,470
<i>♪ I'm a chip off 
The old block! ♪</i>

546
00:44:48,140 --> 00:44:50,060
What do you want, 
Stone? I'm busy.

547
00:44:50,230 --> 00:44:53,230
Doctor, I have a bad 
feeling about this.

548
00:44:53,400 --> 00:44:56,360
I don't think your grandfather's 
been completely honest with us.

549
00:44:57,280 --> 00:44:58,490
<i>There's more to their plan.</i>

550
00:44:59,900 --> 00:45:02,950
How dare you!

551
00:45:03,160 --> 00:45:05,910
You have been jealous of 
my long-lost grand-Pop-Tart

552
00:45:06,120 --> 00:45:08,250
since the very beginning!

553
00:45:08,410 --> 00:45:11,080
I no longer require your 
obsequious groveling.

554
00:45:11,250 --> 00:45:13,710
<i>Consider this your 
notice of termination.</i>

555
00:45:13,880 --> 00:45:17,300
Your letter of reference 
will be L for Loser.

556
00:45:17,460 --> 00:45:19,300
Of course, I'll 
expect you to stay on

557
00:45:19,470 --> 00:45:20,930
until you've been 
successfully cloned.

558
00:45:21,130 --> 00:45:24,600
But you and I are done!

559
00:45:24,760 --> 00:45:27,220
Like a blackened catfish dinner!

560
00:45:27,390 --> 00:45:30,640
Sir, it's too dangerous and 
I'm not there to protect you.

561
00:45:30,810 --> 00:45:31,980
I already lost you once! I...

562
00:45:32,150 --> 00:45:34,270
Unsubscribe. Blocked 
and reported.

563
00:45:35,480 --> 00:45:37,400
I 
can't lose you again.

564
00:45:43,820 --> 00:45:45,410
Do the honors...

565
00:45:46,160 --> 00:45:47,330
grandson.

566
00:45:49,250 --> 00:45:50,540
Here we go.

567
00:47:33,720 --> 00:47:34,730
Sonic!

568
00:47:40,610 --> 00:47:43,650
<i>This is an urgent 
national emergency broadcast.</i>

569
00:47:43,820 --> 00:47:46,280
<i>A spacecraft designed 
by the agency GUN</i>

570
00:47:46,450 --> 00:47:49,370
<i>has been hijacked and launched 
out of the River Thames.</i>

571
00:47:55,160 --> 00:47:58,210
<i>All residents are urged 
to seek immediate shelter.</i>

572
00:48:20,270 --> 00:48:22,520
It's time, Shadow.

573
00:48:24,190 --> 00:48:28,280
Professor, is this really 
what Maria would have wanted?

574
00:48:31,070 --> 00:48:34,410
The question isn't what 
Maria would have wanted.

575
00:48:35,540 --> 00:48:37,540
It's what do they deserve.

576
00:48:38,540 --> 00:48:41,040
Remember what she meant to us.

577
00:48:42,880 --> 00:48:45,800
Remember what they took from us.

578
00:48:56,270 --> 00:48:57,310
Kids!

579
00:48:57,480 --> 00:48:59,390
We have to go, now!

580
00:49:04,610 --> 00:49:07,070
They want to take 
Shadow away from us, Maria!

581
00:49:15,660 --> 00:49:18,370
Hey! Hey! What are you 
doing? Those are children.

582
00:49:18,540 --> 00:49:20,330
- We've got our orders, Walters! 
- Stand down!

583
00:49:44,190 --> 00:49:45,400
Huh?

584
00:49:46,940 --> 00:49:48,030
Maria!

585
00:50:35,530 --> 00:50:38,530
Excuse me, Grand Paso Doble.

586
00:50:38,700 --> 00:50:41,660
What is that thermonuclear 
gerbil doing?

587
00:50:41,830 --> 00:50:44,210
Infusing the core...

588
00:50:44,370 --> 00:50:45,830
with chaos energy.

589
00:50:46,000 --> 00:50:48,630
That's my little secret.

590
00:50:48,790 --> 00:50:51,420
The Eclipse Cannon is 
about to turn this planet

591
00:50:51,590 --> 00:50:54,380
into a flaming pile of rubble,

592
00:50:54,550 --> 00:50:59,390
wiping out everything 
in a 25,000-mile radius.

593
00:51:02,560 --> 00:51:04,730
Including us.

594
00:51:08,650 --> 00:51:09,900
What?

595
00:51:10,820 --> 00:51:13,900
We can't annihilate the Earth!

596
00:51:14,070 --> 00:51:18,530
- Hmm? 
- By combining our genius, we can rule humanity.

597
00:51:18,700 --> 00:51:19,700
Together!

598
00:51:19,780 --> 00:51:22,870
Humanity is a failed experiment.

599
00:51:23,040 --> 00:51:25,290
If anyone should 
know that, it's you.

600
00:51:27,000 --> 00:51:29,920
All your life, you've been 
rejected by this world.

601
00:51:30,800 --> 00:51:32,460
You have nothing down there.

602
00:51:34,050 --> 00:51:36,090
No one who cares about you.

603
00:51:37,890 --> 00:51:39,470
But I have you now.

604
00:51:42,140 --> 00:51:43,560
We're family.

605
00:51:44,480 --> 00:51:46,060
We have each other.

606
00:51:47,560 --> 00:51:48,810
Oh, Ivo...

607
00:51:50,650 --> 00:51:52,360
you're no Maria.

608
00:51:55,690 --> 00:51:59,660
The moment I lost her, my 
family was gone forever!

609
00:52:01,330 --> 00:52:03,040
The only way to give 
Maria's life meaning

610
00:52:03,240 --> 00:52:05,500
is to destroy the world 
that took her from me.

611
00:52:06,370 --> 00:52:08,500
So I'm burning it all down!

612
00:52:11,170 --> 00:52:12,380
It's done.

613
00:52:12,550 --> 00:52:14,840
Good work, Shadow.

614
00:52:15,010 --> 00:52:16,880
I'm prepping the 
firing sequence.

615
00:52:17,050 --> 00:52:20,930
The weapon will be fully 
charged in ten minutes.

616
00:52:24,890 --> 00:52:26,980
It's almost finished, Maria.

617
00:52:27,890 --> 00:52:30,270
You will have justice.

618
00:52:34,650 --> 00:52:35,940
What is that?

619
00:52:36,860 --> 00:52:39,820
Is GUN launching missiles at us?

620
00:52:39,990 --> 00:52:43,030
Impossible. It's 
moving too fast.

621
00:52:46,290 --> 00:52:47,790
It's him.

622
00:52:56,300 --> 00:53:00,590
You hurt my family. 
This ends now!

623
00:53:00,760 --> 00:53:02,470
Now you know my anger.

624
00:53:02,640 --> 00:53:05,510
The pain I've felt for 50 years.

625
00:53:05,680 --> 00:53:08,930
And you've made the 
same choice I did.

626
00:53:09,100 --> 00:53:10,690
I'm nothing like you!

627
00:53:10,850 --> 00:53:11,940
We'll see.

628
00:53:19,780 --> 00:53:21,410
Show yourself, coward!

629
00:53:53,190 --> 00:53:54,860
You were right about one thing.

630
00:53:56,730 --> 00:53:59,070
This ends now.

631
00:54:25,680 --> 00:54:26,720
What's happening?

632
00:54:26,890 --> 00:54:28,010
Where are they?

633
00:54:29,060 --> 00:54:30,310
- Up there. 
- Where?

634
00:54:30,520 --> 00:54:31,520
- Higher. 
- Hmm?

635
00:54:33,140 --> 00:54:34,440
Left yourself open.

636
00:54:34,600 --> 00:54:36,400
Ivo! What are you doing?

637
00:54:36,560 --> 00:54:37,940
Thwarting your evil plan!

638
00:54:48,870 --> 00:54:50,830
- Not the mustache! 
- Agreed.

639
00:54:50,100 --> 00:54:53,710
Let go on three. 
One, two, three!

640
00:54:58,880 --> 00:55:02,130
Oh... a nano-fist.

641
00:55:02,300 --> 00:55:06,010
I haven't seen that since I 
hate-watched <i>Green Lantern</i> in 2011.

642
00:55:06,180 --> 00:55:08,140
I was saving it for Comic-Con.

643
00:55:08,300 --> 00:55:10,350
But now there won't 
be a Comic-Con!

644
00:55:32,100 --> 00:55:36,040
Why are you alone? 
Where are your friends?

645
00:55:37,920 --> 00:55:40,290
They tried to stop 
you, didn't they?

646
00:55:40,500 --> 00:55:41,960
But you came anyway.

647
00:55:42,130 --> 00:55:44,590
Your anger was too much.

648
00:55:44,760 --> 00:55:47,510
What kind of hero 
abandons his friends

649
00:55:47,680 --> 00:55:49,720
to pursue revenge?

650
00:56:16,040 --> 00:56:18,420
Go ahead. Finish it!

651
00:56:19,630 --> 00:56:20,830
You didn't let your pain 
change who you are...

652
00:56:30,050 --> 00:56:31,720
What are you doing?

653
00:56:31,890 --> 00:56:34,770
You won. Take your revenge.

654
00:56:36,640 --> 00:56:38,770
There are no winners 
with revenge.

655
00:57:12,470 --> 00:57:14,390
This whole mess is my fault.

656
00:57:14,560 --> 00:57:17,390
I've been so blinded 
by rage, I thought...

657
00:57:17,180 --> 00:57:19,850
I had no choice.

658
00:57:23,400 --> 00:57:25,770
You always have a choice.

659
00:57:30,740 --> 00:57:33,490
But making the right 
one is never easy.

660
00:57:33,660 --> 00:57:35,370
One more thing I learned

661
00:57:35,530 --> 00:57:38,290
is that when you really 
screw something up,

662
00:57:38,500 --> 00:57:39,960
you can't fix it on your own.

663
00:58:08,860 --> 00:58:12,030
I... will... not... 
try...

664
00:58:12,200 --> 00:58:15,160
to stop... my... 
elders... from...

665
00:58:15,320 --> 00:58:17,740
destroying... the... world!

666
00:58:23,370 --> 00:58:25,290
Playtime is over.

667
00:58:34,010 --> 00:58:36,220
There's no going back now.

668
00:58:40,390 --> 00:58:42,770
Set up defense.

669
00:58:44,730 --> 00:58:46,020
Damn you, autocorrect!

670
00:58:51,900 --> 00:58:52,950
Mantis!

671
00:58:54,910 --> 00:58:56,160
Oh!

672
00:58:59,530 --> 00:58:59,700
Whee!

673
00:59:02,750 --> 00:59:05,330
I'm right here, arach-nerd.

674
00:59:15,840 --> 00:59:18,550
That's what I call 
mantis-scaping.

675
00:59:18,760 --> 00:59:21,180
That's elder abuse!

676
00:59:27,270 --> 00:59:30,480
<i>Alert! Alert! Alert!</i>

677
00:59:30,650 --> 00:59:32,070
Shadow...

678
00:59:32,230 --> 00:59:34,860
I see you've chosen betrayal.

679
00:59:36,030 --> 00:59:38,660
And you were once 
so useful to me.

680
01:00:22,450 --> 01:00:23,870
Please, Grampsy,

681
01:00:24,040 --> 01:00:25,790
don't do this!

682
01:00:25,950 --> 01:00:28,040
Sorry, kiddo.

683
01:00:28,210 --> 01:00:31,420
Bring Your Grandkid 
to Work Day is over.

684
01:00:37,630 --> 01:00:39,380
Any last words?

685
01:00:39,550 --> 01:00:42,260
Just one thing...

686
01:00:43,260 --> 01:00:45,350
that I never thought I'd say.

687
01:00:45,520 --> 01:00:47,020
What is it?

688
01:00:47,180 --> 01:00:49,690
"I love you"?

689
01:00:50,310 --> 01:00:51,650
No.

690
01:00:51,810 --> 01:00:53,730
It was something even better.

691
01:00:53,900 --> 01:00:56,110
But I'm not gonna say it if 
that's the way you're gonna be.

692
01:00:56,150 --> 01:00:58,110
Okay. Bye.

693
01:01:11,000 --> 01:01:11,960
Grandchildren.

694
01:01:13,040 --> 01:01:16,670
All the fun and none 
of the responsibility.

695
01:01:18,800 --> 01:01:21,550
Who said life was pointless?

696
01:01:22,340 --> 01:01:25,260
- Huh? 
- Oh, right. You did.

697
01:01:31,100 --> 01:01:32,770
Victory!

698
01:01:32,810 --> 01:01:35,150
Say what you want 
about my granddad,

699
01:01:35,320 --> 01:01:37,150
he made one hell 
of a bug zapper.

700
01:01:39,360 --> 01:01:41,200
We got to stop that laser!

701
01:01:41,360 --> 01:01:43,570
I knew there was something 
I was forgetting.

702
01:02:10,770 --> 01:02:12,600
We can't stop the 
cannon from firing...

703
01:02:12,770 --> 01:02:14,860
But we can steer it 
away from the Earth.

704
01:02:15,060 --> 01:02:17,400
- Coming around to starboard. 
- Aye-aye, Doc.

705
01:02:21,360 --> 01:02:23,410
Here we go.

706
01:02:24,610 --> 01:02:26,490
It's a little tight.

707
01:02:27,240 --> 01:02:29,450
Definitely not power steering.

708
01:02:35,380 --> 01:02:38,300
Keep... turning.

709
01:02:40,880 --> 01:02:42,720
Jump in anytime here, guys!

710
01:03:05,160 --> 01:03:06,320
Yes!

711
01:03:06,490 --> 01:03:08,740
I did it! I did it!

712
01:03:12,040 --> 01:03:13,750
- Oh! 
- Ooh!

713
01:03:14,410 --> 01:03:15,540
Look what you did!

714
01:03:15,710 --> 01:03:18,340
- Hey, look down there! 
- Sonic!

715
01:03:24,420 --> 01:03:26,510
Oh, Knuckles, please 
tell me you have a...

716
01:03:26,680 --> 01:03:28,390
Last one.

717
01:03:28,550 --> 01:03:29,930
Let's make it count.

718
01:03:32,520 --> 01:03:33,640
Ready for a little base of ball?

719
01:03:35,600 --> 01:03:37,190
Deep breath.

720
01:03:37,400 --> 01:03:40,070
One... two... three!

721
01:04:01,920 --> 01:04:04,050
- Really! 
- What's happening?

722
01:04:04,210 --> 01:04:06,720
The reactor core is overloading.

723
01:04:06,880 --> 01:04:09,220
It's only a matter of 
time before it blows.

724
01:04:09,430 --> 01:04:11,140
So what does that 
mean for Earth?

725
01:04:11,300 --> 01:04:13,970
A radioactive atmosphere.

726
01:04:14,140 --> 01:04:16,640
Rain that kills the crops 
and melts your flesh.

727
01:04:16,810 --> 01:04:18,060
Other than that...

728
01:04:18,230 --> 01:04:19,900
We're not done here!

729
01:04:20,060 --> 01:04:21,980
You try to stabilize 
the reactor.

730
01:04:22,150 --> 01:04:23,400
Buy me some time.

731
01:04:23,570 --> 01:04:25,610
I'll push the station 
away from Earth

732
01:04:25,780 --> 01:04:27,200
before it explodes.

733
01:04:27,400 --> 01:04:31,410
This is our last chance 
to do the right thing.

734
01:04:33,030 --> 01:04:35,660
Go with God

735
01:04:35,830 --> 01:04:38,040
stinking hedgehog.

736
01:04:39,290 --> 01:04:40,750
<i>Core integrity failing.</i>

737
01:04:50,800 --> 01:04:52,470
I've got you, Sonic!

738
01:05:25,800 --> 01:05:29,170
<i>Initializing 
reactor core stabilizers.</i>

739
01:05:47,900 --> 01:05:50,610
This is Doctor Ivo Robotnik,

740
01:05:50,780 --> 01:05:53,530
dedicating my final livestream

741
01:05:53,700 --> 01:05:56,410
to one very special henchman:

742
01:05:57,040 --> 01:05:58,410
<i>Agent Stone.</i>

743
01:05:58,620 --> 01:06:00,830
No, no. Doctor, wait!

744
01:06:00,100 --> 01:06:03,380
<i>If I can't rule the world...</i>

745
01:06:04,380 --> 01:06:06,210
I might as well save it...

746
01:06:06,380 --> 01:06:09,550
for the one and only person 
who ever cared about me.

747
01:06:09,710 --> 01:06:11,630
Don't do this, Doctor, please!

748
01:06:11,800 --> 01:06:15,390
Stone, you were more 
than a sycophant to me.

749
01:06:18,260 --> 01:06:18,680
You were...

750
01:06:21,020 --> 01:06:21,640
a syco-friend.

751
01:06:28,110 --> 01:06:31,650
I'll miss your lattes with 
steamed Austrian goat milk.

752
01:06:33,610 --> 01:06:35,450
I love the way you make 'em!

753
01:07:18,580 --> 01:07:22,370
So... I guess there's only 
one thing left to say.

754
01:07:27,170 --> 01:07:28,670
It's been a real drag.

755
01:07:29,340 --> 01:07:30,840
Thanks for nothing.

756
01:07:49,400 --> 01:07:50,610
Sonic, look.

757
01:08:05,080 --> 01:08:06,710
Goodbye, Doctor.

758
01:08:22,560 --> 01:08:24,060
Let's do this!

759
01:08:24,220 --> 01:08:26,390
Yeah!

760
01:08:26,560 --> 01:08:29,650
All right, 
boys, try and keep up.

761
01:10:26,100 --> 01:10:29,600
Sonic the Hedgehog is 
Family Champion once again!

762
01:10:30,270 --> 01:10:31,310
Tails?

763
01:10:32,310 --> 01:10:34,440
Knuckles?

764
01:10:35,060 --> 01:10:38,020
Okay. Yeah, I overshot 
the finish line.

765
01:10:46,950 --> 01:10:49,950
Okay, so 
how do I get back?

766
01:11:02,170 --> 01:11:03,090
Pro Tip

767
01:11:05,010 --> 01:11:06,640
you'd better not miss.

768
01:11:20,650 --> 01:11:22,650
That's a neat trick.

769
01:11:34,580 --> 01:11:36,500
What? Who are you?
